    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d188">

                <pb facs="0320" n="278" sameAs="frus:frus1863p1/pg278"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Adams.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 586.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-05-07"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >May</hi> 7, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Your despatch of April 24th (No. 389) has
                    been received, together with its accompaniment, a renewed correspondence between
                    Earl Russell and yourself concerning the case of the Sumter.</p>
                <p>The positions you have maintained in your reply to his lordship are approved, and
                    we cannot but hope that upon further consideration they will be conceded by her
                    Majesty’s government.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams</hi>, Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
